# Mac remote build scripts — target configuration.
#
# These variables configure apps/connector.mac/Scripts/mac-build.sh and the iOS
# scripts in apps/web-ui/tools/{ios-build-mac,ios-debug-mac}.sh.
# Copy the lines you need into apps/connector.mac/.env (gitignored) or export them in
# your shell. There are NO repo-specific defaults in the scripts: if neither a
# host nor a host selector resolves, the scripts fail fast with an actionable
# error naming the missing variable.
#
# Precedence: an explicitly-set environment variable always wins over the
# values in apps/connector.mac/.env. For the host specifically:
#   1. an explicitly-set MEMORY_MAC_HOST (highest);
#   2. else MEMORY_MAC_HOST_NAME (selector) -> MEMORY_MAC_HOST_<NAME>;
#   3. else a MEMORY_MAC_HOST set in this file (single-host);
#   4. else fail fast.

# SSH host of the Mac build machine. Required (unless you use the named-host
# selector below).
# An explicitly EMPTY value (MEMORY_MAC_HOST=) means "local destination" and is
# intended for tests / --dry-run only; unset is an error.
# Example (this repo's own Mac):
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST=mcj-mini
MEMORY_MAC_HOST=

# Project directory on the Mac. Required: absolute or ~-rooted, no spaces.
# Example (this repo's own Mac checkout):
# MEMORY_MAC_PATH=~/code/emergent.memory
MEMORY_MAC_PATH=

# ---- Named hosts (optional; use instead of a single MEMORY_MAC_HOST) ------
#
# If you have MULTIPLE Mac build machines (each with its own Xcode), define one
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_<NAME>=<ssh-target> entry per host, then pick which one to
# target by setting MEMORY_MAC_HOST_NAME=<name>. The <name> is normalized
# deterministically: uppercased with every non-alphanumeric character replaced
# by '_'. So "tool", "mini-2" and "Mac Pro" map to MEMORY_MAC_HOST_TOOL,
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_MINI_2 and MEMORY_MAC_HOST_MAC_PRO respectively.
#
# Each named host may also have its own project dir via MEMORY_MAC_PATH_<NAME>
# (same normalization); it overrides MEMORY_MAC_PATH for that host. If omitted,
# MEMORY_MAC_PATH is used.
#
# Example — two hosts, switch by changing the selector:
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_TOOL=mcj@tool
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_MINI=mcj-mini
# MEMORY_MAC_PATH_TOOL=~/code/emergent.memory
# MEMORY_MAC_PATH_MINI=~/code/emergent.memory.mini
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_NAME=tool      # pick "tool" (or "mini")
# MEMORY_MAC_HOST_NAME=

# Optional: override the per-script remote subtree.
#   ios-build-mac.sh / ios-debug-mac.sh default to client/ios
#   mac-build.sh                        defaults to client/macos
# Must be relative to MEMORY_MAC_PATH and must not contain '.' or '..'.
# MEMORY_MAC_SUBTREE=client/ios

# Back-compat alias used by the iOS scripts for the subtree.
# MEMORY_MAC_IOS_SUBDIR=client/ios

# Danger overrides — refuse to sync into a real git clone by default because
# --delete could remove tracked files.
# ALLOW_SYNC_INTO_GIT=1
# ALLOW_DELETE_IN_GIT=1
